1. [THEOREM] Universal Quantification Distributes Over Conjunction (Right)
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Basic
Name: forall_and_right
Description: Let $\alpha$ be a nonempty type, $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$ be a predicate on $\alpha$, and $q$ be a proposition. The universal quantification $\forall x, p(x) \land q$ holds if and only if both $\forall x, p(x)$ holds and $q$ holds.
Signature:  [Nonempty α] (p : α → Prop) (q : Prop) : (∀ x, p x ∧ q) ↔ (∀ x, p x) ∧ q

2. [THEOREM] Left distributive identity: $a(1 + b) = a + ab$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs
Name: mul_one_add
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a type $\alpha$ with multiplication and addition satisfying the left distributive property, we have $a \cdot (1 + b) = a + a \cdot b$.
Signature:  [LeftDistribClass α] (a b : α) : a * (1 + b) = a + a * b

3. [THEOREM] Distributivity of Existential Quantifier over Disjunction in Membership Context
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Basic
Name: exists_mem_or_left
Description: For any predicates $p$, $q$, and $r$ on a type, the following equivalence holds:
\[
(\exists x, (p(x) \lor q(x)) \land r(x)) \leftrightarrow (\exists x, p(x) \land r(x)) \lor (\exists x, q(x) \land r(x))
\]
Signature:  : (∃ (x : _) (_ : p x ∨ q x), r x) ↔ (∃ (x : _) (_ : p x), r x) ∨ ∃ (x : _) (_ : q x), r x

4. [THEOREM] Universal Quantifier Distributes Over Disjunction (Right)
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Basic
Name: forall_or_right
Description: For any proposition $q$ and any predicate $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$, the following are equivalent:
1. For all $x \in \alpha$, either $p(x)$ holds or $q$ holds.
2. Either for all $x \in \alpha$, $p(x)$ holds, or $q$ holds.
Signature:  {q} {p : α → Prop} : (∀ x, p x ∨ q) ↔ (∀ x, p x) ∨ q

5. [THEOREM] Universal Quantifier Distributivity over Disjunction (Left)
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Basic
Name: forall_or_left
Description: For any proposition $q$ and any predicate $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$, the following are equivalent:
1. For all $x \in \alpha$, either $q$ holds or $p(x)$ holds.
2. Either $q$ holds or for all $x \in \alpha$, $p(x)$ holds.

In symbols: $(\forall x, q \lor p(x)) \leftrightarrow (q \lor (\forall x, p(x))$.
Signature:  {q} {p : α → Prop} : (∀ x, q ∨ p x) ↔ q ∨ ∀ x, p x

6. [THEOREM] Universal Quantifier Distributes Over Conjunction (Left Case)
Module: Mathlib.Logic.Basic
Name: forall_and_left
Description: Let $\alpha$ be a nonempty type and let $q$ be a proposition, $p : \alpha \to \text{Prop}$ be a predicate. Then the following are equivalent:
1. For all $x \in \alpha$, both $q$ and $p(x)$ hold.
2. $q$ holds and for all $x \in \alpha$, $p(x)$ holds.

In symbols:
$$(\forall x \in \alpha, q \land p(x)) \leftrightarrow (q \land \forall x \in \alpha, p(x))$$
Signature:  [Nonempty α] (q : Prop) (p : α → Prop) : (∀ x, q ∧ p x) ↔ (q ∧ ∀ x, p x)
