1. [DEFINITION] Pattern-matching case analysis tactic
Module: Mathlib.Tactic.CasesM
Name: Mathlib.Tactic.casesM
Description: The `casesm` tactic performs case analysis (`cases`) on hypotheses whose types match given patterns. It has several variants:
1. `casesm p` applies `cases` to any hypothesis `h : type` where `type` matches pattern `p`
2. `casesm p₁, ..., pₙ` applies `cases` to hypotheses matching any of the patterns
3. `casesm* p` efficiently repeats `casesm p` until no more matches are found
4. `casesm! p` only applies `cases` when it produces at most one subgoal

Example usage: `casesm* _ ∨ _, _ ∧ _` destructs all conjunctions and disjunctions in the current context.
Signature:  : Lean.ParserDescr✝

