1. [THEOREM] Value of Semiconjugate Map at Numerals ≥ 2: $f(n) = f(0) + n \cdot b$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.AddConstMap.Basic
Name: AddConstMapClass.map_ofNat'
Description: Let $G$ be an additive monoid with a multiplicative identity $1$, $H$ an additive monoid, and $b \in H$ a fixed element. For any map $f \colon G \to H$ in the class of semiconjugate maps satisfying $f(x + 1) = f(x) + b$ for all $x \in G$, and for any natural number $n \geq 2$, we have:
\[ f(n) = f(0) + n \cdot b. \]
Signature:  [AddMonoidWithOne G] [AddMonoid H] [AddConstMapClass F G H 1 b] (f : F) (n : ℕ) [n.AtLeastTwo] :
