3. [THEOREM] Semiconjugate Additive Map Property for Integer Scalar Addition
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.AddConstMap.Basic
Name: AddConstMapClass.map_zsmul_add
Description: Let $G$ be an additive commutative group, $H$ an additive group, and $a \in G$, $b \in H$ fixed elements. For any semiconjugate additive map $f \colon G \to H$ with parameters $(a,b)$ (i.e., satisfying $f(x + a) = f(x) + b$ for all $x \in G$), any integer $n \in \mathbb{Z}$, and any $x \in G$, we have:
\[ f(n \cdot a + x) = f(x) + n \cdot b. \]
Signature:  [AddCommGroup G] [AddGroup H] [AddConstMapClass F G H a b] (f : F) (n : ℤ) (x : G) : f (n • a + x) = f x + n • b

